  "chapter": {
    "number": 82,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(83) A Song of a Psalm for Asaph."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, who shall be compared to you? be not silent, neither be still, O God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For behold, your enemies have made a noise; and they that hate you have lifted up the head.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Against your people they have craftily imagined a device, and have taken counsel against your saints.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have said, Come, and let us utterly destroy them out of the nation; and let the name of Israel be remembered no more at all.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For they have taken counsel together with one consent: they have made a confederacy against you;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "even the tents of the Idumeans, and the Ismaelites; Moab, and the Agarenes;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalec; the Philistines also, with them that dwell at Tyre.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yes, Assur too is come with them: they have become a help to the children of Lot. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Do you to them as to Madiam, and to Sisera; as to Jabin at the brook of Kison.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They were utterly destroyed at Aendor: they became as dung for the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Make their princes as Oreb and Zeb, and Zebee and Salmana; even all their princes:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who said, let us take to ourselves the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 155
          },
          {
            "text": "altar of God as an inheritance.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O my God, make them as a wheel; as stubble before the face of the wind.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As fire which shall burn up a wood, as the flame may consume the mountains;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "so shall you persecute them with your tempest, and trouble them in your anger.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Fill their faces with dishonor; so shall they seek your name, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let them be ashamed and troubled for evermore; yes, let them be confounded and destroyed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And let them know that your name is Lord; that you alone are Most High over all the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 155,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Alex. sanctuary.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 82,
          "verse": 12
        }
      }
    ]
  },
